 That year Elkanah went {to Shiloh} to offer sacrifices and to keep the promises he made to God. He took his family with him. </v>
      <v n="22">
 But Hannah did not go. She told Elkanah, “When the boy is old enough to eat solid food, I will take him to Shiloh. Then I will give him to the Lord. He will become a Nazirite. [12] [13] He will stay there at Shiloh. </v>
      <v n="23">
 Hannah’s husband Elkanah said to her, “Do what you think is best. You may stay home until the boy is old enough to eat solid food. May the Lord do what you have said.” So Hannah stayed at home to nurse her son until he was old enough to eat solid food. </v>
      <v n="24">
 When the boy was old enough to eat solid food, Hannah took him to the Lord’s house at Shiloh. Hannah also took a bull that was three years old, 20 pounds [14] of flour, and a bottle of wine. </v>
      <v n="25">
 They went before the Lord. Elkanah killed the bull as a sacrifice to the Lord like he usually did. [15] Then Hannah gave the boy to Eli. </v>
