but they won’t escape their troubles.
Their hope leads only to death.”
 </v>
    </c>
    <c n="12">
      <v n="1">
 Then Job answered {them}: </v>
      <v n="2">
 “I’m sure you think you are
the only wise people.
You think when you die,
wisdom will be gone with you.
 </v>
      <v n="3">
 But my mind is as good as yours.
I am as smart as you are.
Anyone can see this is true.
 </v>
      <v n="4">
 “My friends laugh at me now.
They say,
‘He prayed to God,
and he got his answer.
{That is why all these bad things
happened to him.}’
 </v>
      <v n="5">
 People that don’t have troubles
make fun of people who do have them.
Those people hit a man when he is down.
 </v>
      <v n="6">
 But robbers’ tents are not bothered.
People who make God angry live in peace,
and their own strength
is their only god!
 </v>
      <v n="7">
 “But ask the animals,
they will teach you.
Or ask the birds of the air,
they will tell you.
 </v>
      <v n="8">
 Or speak to the earth,
it will teach you.
Or let the fish in the sea
tell you their wisdom.
 </v>
      <v n="9">
