 </v>
      <v n="27">
 Are you the one who told the eagle [94] 
to fly high into the sky.
Did you tell him to build his nest
high in the mountains?
 </v>
      <v n="28">
 The eagle lives on a cliff.
The cliff is the eagle’s fortress. [95] 
 </v>
      <v n="29">
 An eagle watches for his food
from high in his fortress.
An eagle can see food that is far away.
 </v>
      <v n="30">
 Eagles will gather where the dead bodies are.
 </v>
    </c>
    <c n="40">
      <v n="1">
 The Lord answered Job and said to him:
 </v>
      <v n="2">
 “Job, you argued with God All-Powerful.
