 </v>
      <v n="18">
 The Lord showed me that the men of Anathoth [99] were making plots against me. The Lord showed me the things they were doing, so I knew they were against me. </v>
      <v n="19">
 Before the Lord showed me that the people were against me, I was like a gentle lamb waiting to be butchered. I did not understand that they were against me. They were saying these things about me: “Let us destroy the tree and its fruit! Let us kill him! Then people will forget him.” </v>
      <v n="20">
 But Lord, you are a fair judge. You know how to test peoples’ hearts and minds. I will tell you my arguments. And I will let you give them the punishment they deserve. </v>
