 Then I heard the same voice from heaven again. The voice said to me, “Go and take the open scroll [77] that is in the angel’s hand. This is the angel that is standing on the sea and on the land.” </v>
      <v n="9">
 So I went to the angel and asked him to give me the little scroll. [78] The angel said to me, “Take the scroll and eat it. It will be sour in your stomach. But in your mouth it will be sweet like honey.” </v>
      <v n="10">
 So I took the little scroll from the angel’s hand. I ate the scroll. In my mouth it tasted sweet like honey. But after I ate it, it was sour in my stomach. </v>
      <v n="11">
 Then I was told, “You must prophesy [79] again about many races of people, many nations, languages, and rulers.” </v>
